## ---------------------------------------------------------------
## Spherical inclusion embedded in a full cubic matrix
## ---------------------------------------------------------------

reset
undo group begin

## Geometry
sphere radius 1                      ## the inclusion, kept
brick x 8                            ## the matrix
sphere radius 1                      ## sacrificial cutting tool

## Hollow out the matrix. The boolean result may take a new id,
## so compress to force inclusion -> 1, matrix -> 2.
subtract volume 3 from volume 2
compress ids
list volume                          ## expect exactly 2 volumes

## Keep temporary two-block membership so scheme assignment survives webcuts.
block 1 volume 1
block 2 volume 2

## Partition into octants for meshability
webcut volume all with plane xplane
webcut volume all with plane yplane
webcut volume all with plane zplane

## Sidesets AFTER the webcuts, picked geometrically
sideset 1 surface with x_coord < -3.999
sideset 1 name "xmin"

## Enforce a contiguous mesh across the inclusion/matrix interface
imprint volume all
merge all

## Mesh schemes by temporary blocks (applies to all split child volumes).
volume in block 1 scheme tetprimitive
volume in block 2 scheme polyhedron

## Mesh size
volume all size 0.2

## Generate the mesh
mesh volume all

## Collapse to one exported element block for thermal input convention.
delete block 1
delete block 2
block 1 hex all
block 1 name "eblock-0_0_0"

undo group end

## Sanity checks
list block all
quality volume all

export Genesis "mesh.exo" dimension 3 block 1 overwrite